WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.360
Buyers invited to order Tesla's 29,990$ cybercab must pay at $299 monthly fee before the vehicle can operate at all. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 665. After the order window, the purchase restrictions, a Texas solar factory, and a Europe software change, then first principles. Tesla is inviting select customers to order the steering wheel free two-seater inside EVs reports, with the first month of that required subscription free.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.560
Deliveries are expected to begin as soon as December and only in supported service areas.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:40.680
The vehicle is positioned as Tesla's cheapest model, undercutting the Model 3 by $7,000.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:46.040
Sales are to handpicked buyers at least to start, and initial availability is limited.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.240
It is not clear when or if those sales will expand to the general public.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:56.710
The CyberCab purchase agreement, detailed by Drive Tesla Canada, sets strict rules on ownership

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:57.490
and operation.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:02.210
Personal units cannot join the Robotaxi network without Tesla authorization.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:08.150
Elon Musk, responding on X as reported by the Supercar blog, said the monthly fee should

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:13.190
sit closer to full self-driving or FSD and connectivity on other models.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.650
Those two services together come to around $115 per month.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:22.290
He said the offer would expand nationwide as regulatory approvals come through.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.690
Tesla wants to begin public sales of the CyberCab by the end of this year.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:32.630
The vehicle is expected to operate unsupervised in the same approved areas as Tesla's Robotaxi

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.950
service, which has expanded from Austin to several other United States cities.

00:01:37.914 --> 00:01:40.594
Tesla shared the CyberCab Order Agreement details.

00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:46.394
Tesla Roddy reported, and customer-owned units can operate inside the same geofences as

00:01:46.394 --> 00:01:47.574
the Robotaxi service.

00:01:48.154 --> 00:01:53.614
A safety probe, Urban Acres reports, continues even as limited CyberCab orders open.

00:01:53.614 --> 00:02:00.550
Crews broke ground on a plan $10 billion Tesla Solar Factory in Texas, Yahoo Finance Reports,

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:06.210
a project that could expand domestic panel production. The project is still in the site preparation

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:13.970
stage, with commercial production set for 2029. The site covers roughly 3,000 acres in Fort Bend County.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:18.750
Drone footage shows a homestead still in use alongside equipment staging areas.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:24.350
Silicone ingots and wafers, coated cells, and finished solar modules would all be made

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:29.330
within the same manufacturing operation, identified as Project Crystal Sun in public

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.890
filing submitted in July, under the State's Jobs, Energy, Technology, and Innovation Act.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:41.350
Tesla CEO Elon Musk has said Tesla and SpaceX may each manufacture 100 gigawatts of solar

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.330
products annually in the United States.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:49.286
Europe is receiving a software update that rebrands FSD as Tesla assisted driving.

00:02:49.826 --> 00:02:55.326
The Tesla Motors subreddit reports, the same update caps the speed offset at 10%.

00:02:55.326 --> 00:03:01.066
An expanded Tesla charging site now has 28 bays, the driven reports, and it reclaims

00:03:01.066 --> 00:03:05.786
the title of Australia's largest electric vehicle, or EV, fast charging location.

00:03:06.446 --> 00:03:12.366
Tesla is discounting select inventory vehicles by nearly $5,000, with the cuts applied to

00:03:12.366 --> 00:03:17.166
certain in-stock models. The Securities and Exchange Commission, or SEC, has

00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:22.266
asked a judge, Hoodline Reports, to close the $40 million Musk Tesla Fraud

00:03:22.266 --> 00:03:27.266
Settlement Fund. In brief, German intelligence, Tempo.co English reported,

00:03:27.766 --> 00:03:31.926
has issued a warning that Tesla vehicles carry spy risks. The Wall Street

00:03:31.926 --> 00:03:36.546
Journal reported Tesla opening CyberCab sales to select customers. Clean

00:03:36.546 --> 00:03:41.166
Technica reported Tesla has begun selling the CyberCab at the $30,000 price

00:03:41.166 --> 00:03:46.346
point. Business Today Malaysia reported Tesla has started taking orders for the CyberCab.

00:03:46.806 --> 00:03:53.066
CarSaus reported Tesla is selling the 2027 CyberCab with a required monthly subscription.

00:03:53.686 --> 00:03:58.326
Privately owned CyberCabs are being compared to early foldable phones, T.S. Alamming

00:03:58.326 --> 00:04:03.366
wrote, with first generations that felt rough and later iterations that became daily drivers.

00:04:04.364 --> 00:04:09.964
Wireless charging via a home pad is shown. Personal owner charging details remain unanswered

00:04:09.964 --> 00:04:11.584
ahead of those December deliveries.

00:04:12.144 --> 00:04:17.044
A cybercab requires an active subscription to move at all, unlike a Model Y, where

00:04:17.044 --> 00:04:18.344
FSD can be skipped.

00:04:18.944 --> 00:04:23.384
Approvals remain outside Tesla's control, so owners should watch the Robotaxi map.

00:04:24.024 --> 00:04:27.924
Once authorized, a cybercab could earn back its fee while the owner works.

00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:33.598
The more common solar supply chain splits ingots, cells, and modules across separate

00:04:33.598 --> 00:04:38.498
suppliers in different states or countries, and a single-site complex changes that capital

00:04:38.498 --> 00:04:38.718
map.

00:04:38.718 --> 00:04:44.118
The United States Solar Manufacturing Capacity is expanding, but still trails global leaders,

00:04:44.618 --> 00:04:48.658
and this factor is being framed as one of the larger domestic efforts to consolidate

00:04:48.658 --> 00:04:49.278
that chain.

00:04:50.225 --> 00:04:54.925
Tesla projects roughly 1900 permanent positions when operations begin.

00:04:55.565 --> 00:05:00.645
That headcount is projected to grow to 9,712 by 2033.

00:05:01.345 --> 00:05:05.985
Construction employment is expected to peak at 1,147 jobs.

00:05:05.985 --> 00:05:11.885
An economic analysis accompanying the proposal estimated that Project Crystal Sun could contribute

00:05:11.885 --> 00:05:16.125
$107 billion to the state's gross domestic product over decades.

00:05:17.177 --> 00:05:21.097
For Tesla's energy business, the factory is meant to follow the company's own demand

00:05:21.097 --> 00:05:26.177
from Megapack, Powerwall, and solar roof deployments rather than external suppliers.

00:05:26.797 --> 00:05:31.397
Those outside suppliers can see pricing and availability shift with trade policy or

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.617
raw material shortages.

00:05:32.617 --> 00:05:39.857
The long horizon bet is that integrated United States production can compete on cost once the initial capital is deployed.

00:05:40.397 --> 00:05:47.697
The test is how quickly site preparation turns into finished modules at the volumes needed for both vehicle and stationary storage lines.

00:05:48.615 --> 00:05:57.235
Before we go, the dated step still ahead is Tesla's target of public cybercab sales by the end of this year, as those regulatory approvals come through.

00:05:57.235 --> 00:06:04.455
that covers it for today's Tesla developments. TSLA closed Friday at $390.22

00:06:04.455 --> 00:06:11.915
down $7.23 or 1.8%. Share this episode with a fellow Tesla enthusiast if you

